From 882d000b49077b47c17c175d1c7eaae65c27d3a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:34:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/106] A new Song doesn't play "reversed": initialize the
 TimelineCounter's direction

PR #4445 moved currentlyPlayingReversed and sequenceDirectionMode from Clip
to TimelineCounter, so that recording song automation reads the Song's own
flags instead of casting the Song to a Clip (the old E445 in arranger view).
But only Clip sets them; nothing initializes them for the Song. A Song made
in reused memory, as after song changes, took whatever was there: in the
fuzzer's seed 108 (--mode deep, input 488) its flag held 0xED, so recording
song automation from performance view took the "playing reversed" branch of
AutoParam::homogenizeRegion() with the Song's cut point (INT32_MAX) and froze
with E445. In a release build that branch builds a wrong region. Give both
fields default initializers (false, FORWARD).

Test (beta-1.3/tests/repro/song_reversed_emu.py): with 0xED written into the
memory a new Song is made in, the loaded song's flags are false and FORWARD
(before: 0xED).
---
 src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h b/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h
index 7b01d0f3..4850b891 100644
--- a/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h
+++ b/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h
@@ -51,6 +51,9 @@ public:
 	ParamManagerForTimeline paramManager;
 	bool armedForRecording{true};
 
-	bool currentlyPlayingReversed;
-	SequenceDirection sequenceDirectionMode;
+	// Clip sets these; the Song, the other TimelineCounter (song automation), never does. Uninitialized, a Song made in
+	// reused memory could play "reversed": recording song automation then froze with E445 in
+	// AutoParam::homogenizeRegion() (the fuzzer's seed 108)
+	bool currentlyPlayingReversed{false};
+	SequenceDirection sequenceDirectionMode{SequenceDirection::FORWARD};
 };
